      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 9996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-27T19:42:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately I think it\u0027s not. The SkImage ends up in a display list, and that ends up in the IO unref queue so that we make sure to unref all the SkRefCnt objects on a thread that has a current context.\n\nEven if I try to just pass the texture around, to draw it into a canvas I eventually need to make an SkImage out of it, and that SkImage will end up in a display list that goes into the unref queue.",
      "parentUuid": "09c36c52_bbc8b204",
      "revId": "3389d164d4ccffe271f077d12520a80d31c9a904",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "614004e7_f018c576",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 9996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-27T22:49:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The basic problem here ends up being having things as shared pointers that need to be collected on specific threads. I want a way to steal out the bit that needs special thread handling so I can actually handle it on that thread.",
      "parentUuid": "11715a2f_976a6d18",
      "revId": "3389d164d4ccffe271f077d12520a80d31c9a904",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
